      "explanation": "أَخِي is the possessor of كِتَابُ, so its role is مُضَاف إِلَيْهِ — always جَرّ. As one of the five nouns, its جَرّ marker is the long vowel ي, not a short kasra. جَدِيدٌ, describing the whole phrase كِتَابُ أَخِي الطَّالِبِ, is the predicate — the خَبَر — which is رَفْع."
